Z||000012||FieroFanaticus2||10-03-2001||05:24 PM||||I make the 'Ready or not Tot' babies for Nasco International.  These little dolls scream and cry and make horrible noises just like a real baby.  They use them in schools and other places where young kids learn what it's like to have a real baby.  They don't crap their diapers or anything like that, but they are time controlled and use 'keys' that tell a little computer that someone is taking care of them or not.  Our newest creation is an imitation of a Crack Baby, it imitates a baby who was born addicted to Crack and it has a movable neck.  When you shake it too hard you can break the neck.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||OcalaFiero||10-03-2001||05:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroFanaticus2:<BR><B>I make the 'Ready or not Tot' babies for Nasco International.  These little dolls scream and cry and make horrible noises just like a real baby.  They use them in schools and other places where young kids learn what it's like to have a real baby.  They don't crap their diapers or anything like that, but they are time controlled and use 'keys' that tell a little computer that someone is taking care of them or not.  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My wife and I are making the real thing, the "factory" is due to deliver it mid to late December, we're having a girl (not my idea, but as long as she's healthy I'll take it). Now if only we could make one that won't crap it's diapers.....<P>||||reg||1
