Z||000018||8Ball||10-03-2001||11:31 PM||||Even with some of the people I have to deal with, I LOVE my job. <P>I am a pc/network onsite tech. I stay out all day. Go to a differant place or places almost everyday. And am constantly challenged mentally constantly. <P>It Just gives a sense of fullfillment at the end of the day, when the rest of the world can seem bleek.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Hippocrat||10-04-2001||12:19 AM||||Stay away from the Technical support racket...<P>You take a job because you like helping people, but find out that all you can do is convince them that it is someone else's problem (even if you know different). <P>Even if you know how to fix it you cant tell them because of liability issues. They scream at you, and all you want to do is say "I know exactly what you mean". <P>There are of course some people who think everything is your company's problem but these guys are fun. When I'm not in the wrong(My company) then I don't mind hostile people, like I said they are fun.<P>But hey I'm doing support via E-mail now. So I guess I like my job now <P>Still looking for something new though. I get bored way too easily for my own good I think.<p>[This message has been edited by Hippocrat (edited 10-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||GarethWright||10-04-2001||03:24 AM||||I Love my job, I work in a small Laboratory making Nutrient Broth in little glass vials for bacterial testing, used in the oil industry, I work 5 hours a day, 4 days a week, and get $7.35 an hour (which could be better, but I'm in college, so its spending money) but the Lab is Air Conditioned, we take all our orders by Phone (I never even have to TALK to the customers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">), theres 4 of us working there on a Busy day, normally 2 or 3, and we watch TV while we work!  My boss is my best friends Dad, and apart from me its a family run business, we even have his dogs down there most of the time. (cocker spaniels)||||reg||1
